    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nsince #40321, `:restart` clears the arglist in the running instance and never restores it. this is of particular interest to me because my plugin, [quarrel.nvim](https://github.com/yilisharcs/quarrel.nvim), is now being fed an empty arglist to its database.\n\ni'm pretty sure that this is the culprit: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/845b66dd4a50d7b54050990e27919549c331e1bb/runtime/lua/vim/_core/server.lua#L190\n\ni'd like to know if this is the intended behavior or a porting bug.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `$ nvim --clean foo bar baz`\n2. `:arg` (will show \"[foo] bar baz\")\n3. `:restart`\n4. `:arg` (will show nothing)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nthe arglist isn't destroyed.\n\nstep 4 shows \"[foo] bar baz\".\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev-1679+gdcf55c0cec-dirty (i added a flake, mb)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
