            "body": "> can't remember if `%argdelete` is something I suggested but I couldn't find discussion of it. [@nathanzeng](https://github.com/nathanzeng) any idea?\n\nI think the origin here is that it comes from how 'mini.sessions' implemented the `restart`. The reason to choose deleting arguments there is because otherwise the created temporary session file will contain the code to *always* have those arguments open. So sourcing that file will have arguments always present in the buffer list even if they were not there right before the `:restart`.",
